  "slug": "microbe-comprehensive-mapping-583d",
  "summary": "Recent preprints and a database update offer open, reproducible workflows for bacterial genome typing and comparative resources.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is open, computationally accessible tools that organize bacterial genomic data into standardized groups. Robust Cluster Typing uses ribosomal proteins in a Snakemake/Python workflow to assign genomes to species-level clusters, demonstrated on Campylobacter. SNP2Cluster-Py is an open-source Python framework for context-aware core SNP clustering of pathogen isolates, tested on Klebsiella and pneumococcal WGS datasets. P2CS-Web is an updated resource linking prokaryotic two-component system repertoires to domain architectures, genomic neighbourhoods and sequence clusters. The items differ in scope: two are preprints presenting analysis workflows, while P2CS-Web is a curated database update. What is new is the pathogen-agnostic, reproducible treatment of species designation and transmission-cluster analysis from whole-genome data, with ribosomal proteins as the basis for species assignment in the first item.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-22"
}
